        'The study will demonstrate whether early structured pedagogy successfully accelerates foundational learning and reduces reliance on remedial programmes like Catch Up. By providing rigorous evidence on learning gains, cost-effectiveness, and implementation barriers, the evaluation aims to directly inform national policy decisions and future scaling strategies in Zambia. The findings will be shared through collaborative stakeholder feedback loops and a policy brief designed for education decision-makers and practitioners. Additionally, the insights will be disseminated widely through an open-access academic journal article co-authored with VVOB to contribute to global education evidence.'
